    "details": "<p><strong>All that you need to know about Crackhunt</strong></p>\n<div class=\"position-relative\">\n<div class=\"blue_un-border-before comp-detail un_editor_text_live expanded\"><strong>Description:</strong>\n<ul>\n<li>Crackhunt is a cybersecurity-based gaming event organized by the ISDF Club at AIT</li>\n<li>The event focuses on problem-solving and security challenges</li>\n<li>Any violation of the rules will result in disqualification</li>\n</ul>\n<strong>Rules:</strong>\n<ul>\n<li>The duration of the event is 3 hours; any levels completed outside this window will not be counted</li>\n<li>Attacking servers of any kind, including DDoS attacks or scripting attacks, will lead to immediate disqualification</li>\n<li>Sharing puzzle answers is strictly prohibited</li>\n<li>Multiple logins using the same ID will result in disqualification</li>\n<li>Posting puzzles or levels on public forums, messaging boards, or similar platforms is not allowed</li>\n<li>Use of LLMs and AI tools is not permitted</li>\n<li>The event will be hosted on the official event website</li>\n</ul>\n<strong>Additional Information:</strong>\n<ul>\n<li>Participants may contact the organizing team for any queries or doubts</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n</div>",
